<title>USA: OfficeMax scotched Staples merger - source.</title>
<headline>OfficeMax scotched Staples merger - source.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government agreed Staples Inc could merge with Office Depot Inc, but the deal fell apart because of problems with a third office superstore chain, OfficeMax Inc, a source believes.</p>
<p>The party, who was close to the talks, believes the proposed deal with the U.S. Federal Trade Commission required divestiture of fewer than 100 stores.  But the agreement was contingent on the stores being purchased by OfficeMax.  No deal was ever made with the OfficeMax chain.</p>
<p>Parties to the talks declined comment.</p>
<p>&quot;I cannot confirm any speculation that the company declined invitations to purchase any stores,&quot; said a spokesman for OfficeMax.  &quot;We have no comment regarding what is going on right now.&quot;</p>
</text>
